  "period_note": "Year-end position from the Annual Report's own multi-year 'Five Years Financial Performance at a Glance' summary table (audited), Solo basis where a Solo/Consolidated split is presented. As a Shariah-based Islamic bank, EXIM Bank reports 'Investment' rather than conventional 'Loans and Advances', and 'Non-Performing Investment (NPI)' rather than 'NPL'. Major asset-quality shock: Gross Non-Performing Investment (NPI) ratio jumped from 3.64% (FY2023) to 28.40% (FY2024) — by far the sharpest single-year deterioration of any bank researched in this dataset — while CAR fell from 14.48% to 9.71% (below the 12.5% regulatory minimum) and ROE collapsed from 10.08% to 1.46%. This coincides with the well-documented post-August-2024 exposure of large related-party lending concentrations (S Alam Group) at EXIM Bank following Bangladesh's 2024 political transition.",
